<title>USA: Nike up amid speculation of Buffett interest.</title>
<headline>Nike up amid speculation of Buffett interest.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nike Inc shares ran up in heavy New York Stock Exchange trade early Wednesday on market speculation Warren Buffett, chairman of Berkshire Hathaway Inc, likes Nike as an investment.</p>
<p>&quot;Apparently, there is something out there about GEICO (Berkshire's insurance unit) owning a big stake. It was probably done (purchased) when everyone panicked,&quot; said a trader, referring to Nike's decline to a recent low early last month of about 51-1/4.</p>
<p>Nike's Class B stock was up 3-1/2 to 63-1/2, after more than 2.4 million shares traded on the NYSE.</p>
